  "_description": "Cross-SDK mandate validity vectors (DCP-09 §3.5.2 rule 4 and §3.6): the helper that checks a mandate_id, local revocation and the validity window. Every helper MUST return each case's expect ({valid} or {valid: false, reason}, the first failing rule) for its mandate, its revoked_mandate_ids and its now (verification_time when absent). The rules, in order: the mandate is a JSON object; mandate_id is a non-empty string; it is not revoked (exact string match); valid_from and valid_until are RFC 3339 instants as in interop_vectors.json#rfc3339, compared in milliseconds, never as text; valid_from is not after valid_until; the verification time lies within the window, both limits included. The helper verifies no signature, schema, scope, chain or trust and authorizes nothing; the mandates are unsigned. An API that cannot take a value (a typed map cannot hold a JSON array) MUST skip the case explicitly, never pass it.",
